  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "OPTIMIZATION ON FLAG MANIFOLDS — A ﬂag is a sequence of nested subspaces.\n\n**OPTIMIZATION ON FLAG MANIFOLDS**\n\n*KE YE, KEN SZE-WAI WONG, AND LEK-HENG LIM*\n\n27 pp, 28 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** A ﬂag is a sequence of nested subspaces. Flags are ubiquitous in numerical analysis, arising in ﬁnite elements, multigrid, spectral, and pseudospectral methods for numerical pde; they arise in the form of Krylov subspaces in matrix computations, and as multiresolution analysis in wavelets constructions. They are common in statistics too — principal component, canonical cor- relation, and correspondence analyses may all be viewed as methods for extracting ﬂags from a data set. The main goal of this article is to develop the tools needed for optimizing over a set of ﬂags, which is a smooth manifold called the ﬂag manifold, and it contains the Grassmannian as the simplest special case.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Flags in numerical analysis; 1.2 Flags in statistics; 1.3 Prior work and our contributions; 1.4 Outline; 2 Basic differential geometry of homogeneous s; 2.1 Lie groups and Lie algebras; 2.2 Homogeneous spaces; 2.3 Geodesic orbit spaces; 2.4 Riemannian notions; 3 Basic differential geometry of flag manifold; 4 Flag manifolds as matrix homogeneous spaces; 4.1 Orthogonal coordinates for the flag manifo; 4.2 Stiefel coordinates for the flag manifold; 5 Flag manifolds as matrix manifolds; 5.1 Projection coordinates for the flag manifo; 5.2 Refined projection coordinates for the fla",
